Yes. I once ascended a character (can't recall which one; a knight,
maybe) with OrangeDSM. I think I might have been trying to go
wishless, or minimize wishes, anyway, and that was the dragon that
left scales.

I guess I have an innate aversion to the "I have to have the perfect
AK" mindset. I've worn BoWW to ascend, too, just because I didn't find
speed boots; I've also worn jumping boots on purpose, on someone's
suggestion, and ascended without reflection too. (These are not all
one ascension, btw. I'm not *that* good! ;-) As long as I have
resistances, AC, HP, MR, MC, etc., I like to try to go with what I
have. I'm not at the "I'd rather die than break a conduct" stage, but
I am at the "let's see how far I can go without wishing for or using a
trick to get perfect equipment" stage. I guess it's a bit of a
challenge, albeit a minor one.

It seems to me that a lot of people get themselves completely tricked
out at the Castle, and then complain about how boring it is to go
through the rest of the game as an unkillable killing machine. Why not
leave things just a touch chancy for a while, and see how it goes? You
can always keep your WoW around to get better equipment if you seem to
need it. Personally, I think a YAAP with a bit of an unorthodox AK is
pretty cool.
